IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `dg-core`
IMPORT `dg2-support`

-- Delaware General Corporation Law, 8 Del. C. ch. 1: sections 121 to 127 (Subchapter II) -- POWERS: general powers, specific powers, powers
-- over securities, ultra vires, degrees, banking, private foundations.
--
-- A grant of power is a relation: the corporation (and its officers, directors and stockholders) hold the power or privilege; whoever
-- would object has no right to stop them. The rules here decide whether the power is held, and on what conditions the text attaches.
-- The text rarely says what happens to an act outside a power (section 124 does), so the rules that test a condition answer
-- TRUE or FALSE only where the text does, and NOTHING where it does not.
-- SEAT: a person who incorporates, directs or holds stock; a stockholder who wants to stop an act outside the corporation's power; an officer
-- or director who might be sued for it. Cross-references taken as inputs: section 109 and section 115 (piece dg1); section 141(a) (this piece);
-- 14 Del. C. section 8530 and chapter 85 (Title 14, not among the inputs); 26 U.S.C. sections 4941 to 4945 and the private foundation status
-- (Title 26, not among the inputs). The text is de-code-t8-ch1-2026-10-01.txt (a plain-text rendering, not the official text).
-- Section 122 and section 147 carry a bracketed note about a session-law application clause; that clause is not in the text.

§ `Section 121: general powers`

-- "In addition to the powers enumerated in § 122 of this title, every corporation, its officers, directors and stockholders shall possess and
-- may exercise all the powers and privileges granted by this chapter or by any other law or by its certificate of incorporation, together
-- with any powers incidental thereto, so far as such powers and privileges are necessary or convenient to the conduct, promotion or attainment
-- of the business or purposes set forth in its certificate of incorporation." Fork F-121-1: "so far as" is read as limiting all of the
-- powers (the granted ones and the incidental ones), because "such powers and privileges" refers back to both. The powers enumerated in
-- section 122 are "in addition": section 122 decides those.
-- src:243 | (a) In addition to the powers enumerated in § 122 of this title, every corporation, its officers, directors and stockholders shall possess and may exercise all the powers and privileges granted by this chapter or by any other law or by its certificate of incorporation, together with any powers incidental thereto, so far as such powers and privileges are necessary or convenient to the conduct, promotion or attainment of the business or purposes set forth in its certificate of incorporation.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 121(a) (src:243)
GIVEN `the power or privilege is granted by this chapter` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the power or privilege is granted by any other law` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the power or privilege is granted by the certificate of incorporation` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the power is incidental to a power or privilege so granted` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the power or privilege is necessary or convenient to the conduct, promotion or attainment of the business or purposes set forth in the certificate of incorporation` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 121(a) the corporation, its officers, directors and stockholders possess and may exercise the power or privilege` `the power or privilege is granted by this chapter` `the power or privilege is granted by any other law` `the power or privilege is granted by the certificate of incorporation` `the power is incidental to a power or privilege so granted` `the power or privilege is necessary or convenient to the conduct, promotion or attainment of the business or purposes set forth in the certificate of incorporation` MEANS
        (   `the power or privilege is granted by this chapter`
         OR `the power or privilege is granted by any other law`
         OR `the power or privilege is granted by the certificate of incorporation`
         OR `the power is incidental to a power or privilege so granted`)
    AND `the power or privilege is necessary or convenient to the conduct, promotion or attainment of the business or purposes set forth in the certificate of incorporation`

-- "Every corporation shall be governed by the provisions and be subject to the restrictions and liabilities contained in this chapter."
-- Every corporation organized under this chapter; for any other corporation the subsection does not say.
-- src:244 | (b) Every corporation shall be governed by the provisions and be subject to the restrictions and liabilities contained in this chapter.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 121(b) (src:244)
GIVEN `the corporation is organized under this chapter` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 121(b) the corporation is governed by the provisions and subject to the restrictions and liabilities of this chapter` `the corporation is organized under this chapter` MEANS
    IF   `the corporation is organized under this chapter`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING

§ `Section 122: specific powers`

DECLARE `s 122 Specific power` IS ONE OF
    `to have perpetual succession by its corporate name, under s 122(1)`
    `to sue and be sued in all courts and to participate in any proceeding in its corporate name, under s 122(2)`
    `to have a corporate seal and to use it, under s 122(3)`
    `to deal in and with real or personal property and to dispose of or encumber its property and assets, under s 122(4)`
    `to appoint officers and agents and to pay or otherwise provide for their compensation, under s 122(5)`
    `to adopt, amend and repeal bylaws in accordance with section 109, under s 122(6)`
    `to wind up and dissolve itself in the manner provided in this chapter, under s 122(7)`
    `to conduct its business, carry on its operations and have offices and exercise its powers within or without this State, under s 122(8)`
    `to make donations for the public welfare or for charitable, scientific or educational purposes, under s 122(9)`
    `to be an incorporator, promoter or manager of other corporations of any type or kind, under s 122(10)`
    `to participate with others in an association of any kind, or in a transaction, undertaking or arrangement, under s 122(11)`
    `to transact any lawful business which the corporation's board of directors finds to be in aid of governmental authority, under s 122(12)`
    `to make contracts, incur liabilities, borrow money, issue its notes, bonds and other obligations, and secure its obligations, under s 122(13)`
    `to lend money for its corporate purposes, under s 122(14)`
    `to invest and reinvest its funds and to take, hold and deal with property as security for funds so loaned or invested, under s 122(14)`
    `to pay pensions and establish and carry out pension, profit sharing, stock option, stock purchase, stock bonus, retirement, benefit, incentive and compensation plans, trusts and provisions, under s 122(15)`
    `to provide insurance for its benefit on the life of a director, officer, employee or stockholder, under s 122(16)`
    `to renounce an interest or expectancy in business opportunities, under s 122(17)`
    `to make contracts with current or prospective stockholders or beneficial owners of stock in their capacity as such, under s 122(18)`

DECLARE `s 122(16) Whose life is insured` IS ONE OF
    `the life of a director, officer or employee of the corporation`
    `the life of a stockholder of the corporation`

DECLARE `s 122 Facts about the power` HAS
    `the corporation was created under this chapter` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the certificate of incorporation states a limited period of duration` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the participation is in a corporation, partnership, limited partnership, joint venture or other association of any kind` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the participation is in a transaction, undertaking or arrangement` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the participating corporation would have power to conduct the transaction, undertaking or arrangement by itself` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the business is lawful` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the board of directors finds the business to be in aid of governmental authority` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the lending is for the corporation's corporate purposes` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the insurance is for the corporation's benefit` IS A BOOLEAN
    `whose life is insured` IS A `s 122(16) Whose life is insured`
    `the insurance on the life of a stockholder is for the purpose of acquiring at the stockholder's death shares of the corporation's stock owned by the stockholder` IS A BOOLEAN

-- "Every corporation created under this chapter shall have power, whether or not so provided in the certificate of incorporation, to:" and
-- the eighteen powers. Only paragraph (1) (a limited period of duration stated in the certificate), (11) (a transaction the corporation could not
-- conduct by itself), (12) (lawful business the board finds in aid of governmental authority), (14) (lending for its corporate purposes) and
-- (16) (insurance) turn on a fact; the rest are held without condition. No power depends on whether the certificate provides for it.
-- For a corporation not created under this chapter the paragraph does not speak: NOTHING.
-- src:248 | Every corporation created under this chapter shall have power, whether or not so provided in the certificate of incorporation, to:
-- src:249 | (1) Have perpetual succession by its corporate name, unless a limited period of duration is stated in its certificate of incorporation;
-- src:250 | (2) Sue and be sued in all courts and participate, as a party or otherwise, in any judicial, administrative, arbitrative or other proceeding, in its corporate name;
-- src:251 | (3) Have a corporate seal, which may be altered at pleasure, and use the same by causing it or a facsimile thereof, to be impressed or affixed or in any other manner reproduced;
-- src:252 | (4) Purchase, receive, take by grant, gift, devise, bequest or otherwise, lease, or otherwise acquire, own, hold, improve, employ, use and otherwise deal in and with real or personal property, or any interest therein, wherever situated, and to sell, convey, lease, exchange, transfer or otherwise dispose of, or mortgage or pledge, all or any of its property and assets, or any interest therein, wherever situated;
-- src:253 | (5) Appoint such officers and agents as the business of the corporation requires and to pay or otherwise provide for them suitable compensation; provided that any contract or other appointment or delegation of authority that empowers an officer or agent to act on behalf of the corporation shall be subject to § 141(a) of this title, to the extent it is applicable;
-- src:254 | (6) Adopt, amend and repeal bylaws in accordance with § 109 of this title;
-- src:255 | (7) Wind up and dissolve itself in the manner provided in this chapter;
-- src:256 | (8) Conduct its business, carry on its operations and have offices and exercise its powers within or without this State;
-- src:257 | (9) Make donations for the public welfare or for charitable, scientific or educational purposes, and in time of war or other national emergency in aid thereof;
-- src:258 | (10) Be an incorporator, promoter or manager of other corporations of any type or kind;
-- src:259 | (11) Participate with others in any corporation, partnership, limited partnership, joint venture or other association of any kind, or in any transaction, undertaking or arrangement which the participating corporation would have power to conduct by itself, whether or not such participation involves sharing or delegation of control with or to others;
-- src:260 | (12) Transact any lawful business which the corporation’s board of directors shall find to be in aid of governmental authority;
-- src:262 | (14) Lend money for its corporate purposes, invest and reinvest its funds, and take, hold and deal with real and personal property as security for the payment of funds so loaned or invested;
-- src:263 | (15) Pay pensions and establish and carry out pension, profit sharing, stock option, stock purchase, stock bonus, retirement, benefit, incentive and compensation plans, trusts and provisions for any or all of its directors, officers and employees, and for any or all of the directors, officers and employees of its subsidiaries;
-- src:264 | (16) Provide insurance for its benefit on the life of any of its directors, officers or employees, or on the life of any stockholder for the purpose of acquiring at such stockholder’s death shares of its stock owned by such stockholder;
@ref 8 Del. C. § 122 (src:248-264)
GIVEN `the power` IS A `s 122 Specific power`
      `the facts` IS A `s 122 Facts about the power`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 122 the corporation has power` `the power` `the facts` MEANS
    IF   NOT `the facts`'s `the corporation was created under this chapter`
    THEN NOTHING
    ELSE CONSIDER `the power`
         WHEN `to have perpetual succession by its corporate name, under s 122(1)` THEN JUST (NOT `the facts`'s `the certificate of incorporation states a limited period of duration`)
         WHEN `to participate with others in an association of any kind, or in a transaction, undertaking or arrangement, under s 122(11)` THEN
             IF   `the facts`'s `the participation is in a corporation, partnership, limited partnership, joint venture or other association of any kind`
             THEN JUST TRUE
             ELSE IF   `the facts`'s `the participation is in a transaction, undertaking or arrangement`
                  THEN JUST (`the facts`'s `the participating corporation would have power to conduct the transaction, undertaking or arrangement by itself`)
                  ELSE NOTHING
         WHEN `to transact any lawful business which the corporation's board of directors finds to be in aid of governmental authority, under s 122(12)` THEN
             JUST (`the facts`'s `the business is lawful` AND `the facts`'s `the board of directors finds the business to be in aid of governmental authority`)
         WHEN `to lend money for its corporate purposes, under s 122(14)` THEN JUST (`the facts`'s `the lending is for the corporation's corporate purposes`)
         WHEN `to provide insurance for its benefit on the life of a director, officer, employee or stockholder, under s 122(16)` THEN
             JUST (   `the facts`'s `the insurance is for the corporation's benefit`
                  AND (CONSIDER `the facts`'s `whose life is insured`
                       WHEN `the life of a director, officer or employee of the corporation` THEN TRUE
                       WHEN `the life of a stockholder of the corporation` THEN `the facts`'s `the insurance on the life of a stockholder is for the purpose of acquiring at the stockholder's death shares of the corporation's stock owned by the stockholder`))
         OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- (5): "any contract or other appointment or delegation of authority that empowers an officer or agent to act on behalf of the corporation
-- shall be subject to § 141(a) of this title, to the extent it is applicable". How far § 141(a) applies is for that section (this piece).
-- src:253 | provided that any contract or other appointment or delegation of authority that empowers an officer or agent to act on behalf of the corporation shall be subject to § 141(a) of this title, to the extent it is applicable;
@ref 8 Del. C. § 122(5) (src:253)
GIVEN `the contract, appointment or delegation empowers an officer or agent to act on behalf of the corporation` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 122(5) the contract, appointment or delegation is subject to section 141(a)` `the contract, appointment or delegation empowers an officer or agent to act on behalf of the corporation` MEANS
    IF   `the contract, appointment or delegation empowers an officer or agent to act on behalf of the corporation`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING

DECLARE `s 122(13) Relationship of the other corporation to the contracting corporation` IS ONE OF
    `a corporation all of the outstanding stock of which is owned, directly or indirectly, by the contracting corporation`
    `a corporation which owns, directly or indirectly, all of the outstanding stock of the contracting corporation`
    `a corporation all of the outstanding stock of which is owned, directly or indirectly, by a corporation which owns, directly or indirectly, all of the outstanding stock of the contracting corporation`
    `a person or entity in some other relationship to the contracting corporation`

-- (13): contracts of guaranty and suretyship "which are necessary or convenient to the conduct, promotion or attainment of the business of
-- (a) a corporation all of the outstanding stock of which is owned, directly or indirectly, by the contracting corporation, or (b) a
-- corporation which owns, directly or indirectly, all of the outstanding stock of the contracting corporation, or (c) a corporation all of
-- the outstanding stock of which is owned, directly or indirectly, by a corporation which owns, directly or indirectly, all of the
-- outstanding stock of the contracting corporation, which contracts of guaranty and suretyship shall be deemed to be necessary or
-- convenient to the conduct, promotion or attainment of the business of the contracting corporation, and make other contracts of guaranty
-- and suretyship which are necessary or convenient to the conduct, promotion or attainment of the business of the contracting
-- corporation". The three related corporations: deemed necessary or convenient. Any other: it must in fact be so; else the text does not say.
-- src:261 | and make contracts of guaranty and suretyship which are necessary or convenient to the conduct, promotion or attainment of the business of (a) a corporation all of the outstanding stock of which is owned, directly or indirectly, by the contracting corporation, or (b) a corporation which owns, directly or indirectly, all of the outstanding stock of the contracting corporation, or (c) a corporation all of the outstanding stock of which is owned, directly or indirectly, by a corporation which owns, directly or indirectly, all of the outstanding stock of the contracting corporation, which contracts of guaranty and suretyship shall be deemed to be necessary or convenient to the conduct, promotion or attainment of the business of the contracting corporation, and make other contracts of guaranty and suretyship which are necessary or convenient to the conduct, promotion or attainment of the business of the contracting corporation;
@ref 8 Del. C. § 122(13) (src:261)
GIVEN `the relationship` IS A `s 122(13) Relationship of the other corporation to the contracting corporation`
      `the contract of guaranty or suretyship is necessary or convenient to the conduct, promotion or attainment of the business of the contracting corporation` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 122(13) the contract of guaranty or suretyship is within the power as necessary or convenient to the business of the contracting corporation` `the relationship` `the contract of guaranty or suretyship is necessary or convenient to the conduct, promotion or attainment of the business of the contracting corporation` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the relationship`
    WHEN `a person or entity in some other relationship to the contracting corporation` THEN
        IF   `the contract of guaranty or suretyship is necessary or convenient to the conduct, promotion or attainment of the business of the contracting corporation`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        ELSE NOTHING
    OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- (17): "Renounce, in its certificate of incorporation or by action of its board of directors, any interest or expectancy of the corporation
-- in, or in being offered an opportunity to participate in, specified business opportunities or specified classes or categories of
-- business opportunities that are presented to the corporation or 1 or more of its officers, directors or stockholders". A renunciation
-- made in the bylaws or elsewhere, a blanket renunciation, or of opportunities not so presented: the text does not say.
