§ `Section 124: lack of corporate capacity or power`

DECLARE `s 124 Proceeding in which lack of capacity or power is raised` IS ONE OF
    `a proceeding by a stockholder against the corporation to enjoin the doing of an act or the transfer of property by or to the corporation`
    `a proceeding by the corporation, directly or through a receiver, trustee or other legal representative, or through stockholders in a representative suit, against an incumbent or former officer or director for loss or damage due to the officer's or director's unauthorized act`
    `a proceeding by the Attorney General to dissolve the corporation, or to enjoin the corporation from the transaction of unauthorized business`
    `a proceeding of any other kind`

-- "No act of a corporation and no conveyance or transfer of real or personal property to or by a corporation shall be invalid by reason of the
-- fact that the corporation was without capacity or power to do such act or to make or receive such conveyance or transfer". The answer to
-- "is it invalid by reason of that fact?" is always FALSE; the act may be invalid for some other reason, which this rule does not decide.
-- src:274 | No act of a corporation and no conveyance or transfer of real or personal property to or by a corporation shall be invalid by reason of the fact that the corporation was without capacity or power to do such act or to make or receive such conveyance or transfer, …
@ref 8 Del. C. § 124 (src:274)
GIVEN `the corporation was without capacity or power to do the act or to make or receive the conveyance or transfer` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 124 the act, conveyance or transfer is invalid by reason of the corporation's lack of capacity or power` `the corporation was without capacity or power to do the act or to make or receive the conveyance or transfer` MEANS
    FALSE

-- "...but such lack of capacity or power may be asserted: (1) In a proceeding by a stockholder against the corporation to enjoin the doing of
-- any act or acts or the transfer of real or personal property by or to the corporation. ... (2) In a proceeding by the corporation, whether
-- acting directly or through a receiver, trustee or other legal representative, or through stockholders in a representative suit, against an
-- incumbent or former officer or director of the corporation, for loss or damage due to such incumbent or former officer's or director's
-- unauthorized act; (3) In a proceeding by the Attorney General to dissolve the corporation, or to enjoin the corporation from the
-- transaction of unauthorized business." Fork F-124-1: the three are read as the only occasions (the rule is "no act invalid, but ... may be
-- asserted in these"); in a proceeding of any other kind the answer is FALSE.
-- src:274 | but such lack of capacity or power may be asserted:
-- src:275 | (1) In a proceeding by a stockholder against the corporation to enjoin the doing of any act or acts or the transfer of real or personal property by or to the corporation. …
-- src:276 | (2) In a proceeding by the corporation, whether acting directly or through a receiver, trustee or other legal representative, or through stockholders in a representative suit, against an incumbent or former officer or director of the corporation, for loss or damage due to such incumbent or former officer’s or director’s unauthorized act;
-- src:277 | (3) In a proceeding by the Attorney General to dissolve the corporation, or to enjoin the corporation from the transaction of unauthorized business.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 124 (src:274-277)
GIVEN `the proceeding` IS A `s 124 Proceeding in which lack of capacity or power is raised`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 124 the lack of capacity or power may be asserted in the proceeding` `the proceeding` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the proceeding`
    WHEN `a proceeding of any other kind` THEN FALSE
    OTHERWISE TRUE

-- (1), second sentence: "If the unauthorized acts or transfer sought to be enjoined are being, or are to be, performed or made pursuant to any
-- contract to which the corporation is a party, the court may, if all of the parties to the contract are parties to the proceeding and if it
-- deems the same to be equitable, set aside and enjoin the performance of such contract". Whether it is equitable is the court's: an input.
-- src:275 | If the unauthorized acts or transfer sought to be enjoined are being, or are to be, performed or made pursuant to any contract to which the corporation is a party, the court may, if all of the parties to the contract are parties to the proceeding and if it deems the same to be equitable, set aside and enjoin the performance of such contract, …
@ref 8 Del. C. § 124(1) (src:275)
GIVEN `the unauthorized acts or transfer sought to be enjoined are being, or are to be, performed or made pursuant to a contract to which the corporation is a party` IS A BOOLEAN
      `all of the parties to the contract are parties to the proceeding` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the court deems it equitable` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 124(1) the court may set aside and enjoin the performance of the contract` `the unauthorized acts or transfer sought to be enjoined are being, or are to be, performed or made pursuant to a contract to which the corporation is a party` `all of the parties to the contract are parties to the proceeding` `the court deems it equitable` MEANS
        `the unauthorized acts or transfer sought to be enjoined are being, or are to be, performed or made pursuant to a contract to which the corporation is a party`
    AND `all of the parties to the contract are parties to the proceeding`
    AND `the court deems it equitable`

-- "...and in so doing may allow to the corporation or to the other parties to the contract, as the case may be, such compensation as may be
-- equitable for the loss or damage sustained by any of them which may result from the action of the court in setting aside and enjoining
-- the performance of such contract, but anticipated profits to be derived from the performance of the contract shall not be awarded by the
-- court as a loss or damage sustained."
-- src:275 | and in so doing may allow to the corporation or to the other parties to the contract, as the case may be, such compensation as may be equitable for the loss or damage sustained by any of them which may result from the action of the court in setting aside and enjoining the performance of such contract, …
@ref 8 Del. C. § 124(1) (src:275)
GIVEN `the court has set aside and enjoined the performance of the contract` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 124(1) the court may allow compensation for loss or damage resulting from setting aside the contract` `the court has set aside and enjoined the performance of the contract` MEANS
    IF   `the court has set aside and enjoined the performance of the contract`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING

-- src:275 | but anticipated profits to be derived from the performance of the contract shall not be awarded by the court as a loss or damage sustained;
@ref 8 Del. C. § 124(1) (src:275)
GIVEN `the profit is an anticipated profit to be derived from the performance of the contract` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 124(1) the court may award the profit as a loss or damage sustained` `the profit is an anticipated profit to be derived from the performance of the contract` MEANS
    NOT `the profit is an anticipated profit to be derived from the performance of the contract`

§ `Section 125: academic or honorary degrees; private business or trade schools`

-- "No corporation organized after April 18, 1945" and "No corporation organized before April 18, 1945": a corporation organized ON that date is in neither.
-- src:281 | No corporation organized after April 18, 1945, shall have power to confer academic or honorary degrees …
@ref 8 Del. C. § 125 (src:281)
GIVETH A DATE
`s 125 April 18, 1945` MEANS YearMonthDay 1945 4 18

-- After 18 April 1945: the certificate or an amendment must so provide, and before being filed must have endorsed on it the approval of the
-- Department of Education. Before it: the corporation may not have the power "without first filing in the office of the Secretary of State a
-- certificate of amendment so providing, the filing of which ... shall be subject to prior approval of the Department of Education, evidenced
-- as hereinabove provided". On the date itself the text does not say: NOTHING.
-- src:281 | No corporation organized after April 18, 1945, shall have power to confer academic or honorary degrees unless the certificate of incorporation or an amendment thereof shall so provide and unless the certificate of incorporation or an amendment thereof prior to its being filed in the office of the Secretary of State shall have endorsed thereon the approval of the Department of Education of this State. No corporation organized before April 18, 1945, any provision in its certificate of incorporation to the contrary notwithstanding, shall possess the power aforesaid without first filing in the office of the Secretary of State a certificate of amendment so providing, the filing of which certificate of amendment in the office of the Secretary of State shall be subject to prior approval of the Department of Education, evidenced as hereinabove provided. …
@ref 8 Del. C. § 125 (src:281)
GIVEN `the date the corporation was organized` IS A DATE
      `the certificate of incorporation or an amendment of it provides that the corporation may confer academic or honorary degrees` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the certificate or amendment, before being filed in the office of the Secretary of State, had endorsed on it the approval of the Department of Education` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the corporation has filed in the office of the Secretary of State a certificate of amendment so providing` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 125 the corporation has power to confer academic or honorary degrees` `the date the corporation was organized` `the certificate of incorporation or an amendment of it provides that the corporation may confer academic or honorary degrees` `the certificate or amendment, before being filed in the office of the Secretary of State, had endorsed on it the approval of the Department of Education` `the corporation has filed in the office of the Secretary of State a certificate of amendment so providing` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF   `the date the corporation was organized` GREATER THAN `s 125 April 18, 1945`
        THEN JUST (   `the certificate of incorporation or an amendment of it provides that the corporation may confer academic or honorary degrees`
                  AND `the certificate or amendment, before being filed in the office of the Secretary of State, had endorsed on it the approval of the Department of Education`)
        IF   `the date the corporation was organized` LESS THAN `s 125 April 18, 1945`
        THEN JUST (   `the corporation has filed in the office of the Secretary of State a certificate of amendment so providing`
                  AND `the certificate or amendment, before being filed in the office of the Secretary of State, had endorsed on it the approval of the Department of Education`)
        OTHERWISE NOTHING

-- "Approval shall be granted only when it appears to the reasonable satisfaction of the Department of Education that the corporation is
-- engaged in conducting a bona fide institution of higher learning, giving instructions in arts and letters, science or the professions,
-- or that the corporation proposes, in good faith, to engage in that field and has or will have the resources, including personnel,
-- requisite for the conduct of an institution of higher learning." A necessary condition only: if it is not met the Department may not
-- grant approval; if it is met the text does not say that the Department must (NOTHING). The satisfaction is the Department's: an input.
-- src:281 | Approval shall be granted only when it appears to the reasonable satisfaction of the Department of Education that the corporation is engaged in conducting a bona fide institution of higher learning, giving instructions in arts and letters, science or the professions, or that the corporation proposes, in good faith, to engage in that field and has or will have the resources, including personnel, requisite for the conduct of an institution of higher learning. …
@ref 8 Del. C. § 125 (src:281)
GIVEN `it appears to the reasonable satisfaction of the Department of Education that the corporation is engaged in conducting a bona fide institution of higher learning, giving instructions in arts and letters, science or the professions` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it appears to the reasonable satisfaction of the Department of Education that the corporation proposes, in good faith, to engage in that field and has or will have the resources, including personnel, requisite for the conduct of an institution of higher learning` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 125 the Department of Education may grant approval` `it appears to the reasonable satisfaction of the Department of Education that the corporation is engaged in conducting a bona fide institution of higher learning, giving instructions in arts and letters, science or the professions` `it appears to the reasonable satisfaction of the Department of Education that the corporation proposes, in good faith, to engage in that field and has or will have the resources, including personnel, requisite for the conduct of an institution of higher learning` MEANS
    IF   `it appears to the reasonable satisfaction of the Department of Education that the corporation is engaged in conducting a bona fide institution of higher learning, giving instructions in arts and letters, science or the professions`
         OR `it appears to the reasonable satisfaction of the Department of Education that the corporation proposes, in good faith, to engage in that field and has or will have the resources, including personnel, requisite for the conduct of an institution of higher learning`
    THEN NOTHING
    ELSE JUST FALSE

-- "Upon dissolution, all such corporations shall comply with § 8530 of Title 14." Title 14 is not among the inputs: whether the corporation
-- has complied is a fact.
-- src:281 | Upon dissolution, all such corporations shall comply with § 8530 of Title 14. Notwithstanding any provision herein to the contrary, no corporation shall have the power to conduct a private business or trade school unless the certificate of incorporation or an amendment thereof, prior to its being filed in the office of the Secretary of State, shall have endorsed thereon the approval of the Department of Education pursuant to Chapter 85 of Title 14.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 125 (src:281)
GIVEN `the corporation is one that has power to confer academic or honorary degrees under this section` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the corporation is dissolving` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 125 the corporation must comply with section 8530 of Title 14` `the corporation is one that has power to confer academic or honorary degrees under this section` `the corporation is dissolving` MEANS
    IF   `the corporation is one that has power to confer academic or honorary degrees under this section` AND `the corporation is dissolving`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING

-- "Notwithstanding any provision herein to the contrary, no corporation shall have the power to conduct a private business or trade school
-- unless the certificate of incorporation or an amendment thereof, prior to its being filed in the office of the Secretary of State, shall
-- have endorsed thereon the approval of the Department of Education pursuant to Chapter 85 of Title 14."
-- out of range: Chapter 85 of Title 14 (not among the inputs): whether the approval was given and endorsed is a plain fact.
-- src:281 | Notwithstanding any provision herein to the contrary, no corporation shall have the power to conduct a private business or trade school unless the certificate of incorporation or an amendment thereof, prior to its being filed in the office of the Secretary of State, shall have endorsed thereon the approval of the Department of Education pursuant to Chapter 85 of Title 14.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 125 (src:281)
GIVEN `the certificate of incorporation or an amendment of it, before being filed in the office of the Secretary of State, had endorsed on it the approval of the Department of Education pursuant to Chapter 85 of Title 14` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 125 the corporation has power to conduct a private business or trade school` `the certificate of incorporation or an amendment of it, before being filed in the office of the Secretary of State, had endorsed on it the approval of the Department of Education pursuant to Chapter 85 of Title 14` MEANS
    `the certificate of incorporation or an amendment of it, before being filed in the office of the Secretary of State, had endorsed on it the approval of the Department of Education pursuant to Chapter 85 of Title 14`

§ `Section 125: a law school corporation`

DECLARE `s 125 Facts about a law school corporation` HAS
    `the corporation is conducting a law school which has its principal place of operation in Delaware` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the corporation intends to meet the standards of approval of the American Bar Association` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the date the corporation began actual operation` IS A DATE
    `the date the corporation retained the dean` IS A DATE
    `the corporation retained the dean at its own expense to make an on-site inspection and report` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the dean or dean emeritus is of a law school fully approved by the American Bar Association` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the dean was chosen by the Attorney General from a panel of 3 deans nominated one each by the trustees of the corporation, a committee of the Student Bar Association and a committee of lawyers who are parents of students, with 2 full professors of accredited law schools substituted for any dean a group could not find` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the dean reported in writing that, in the dean's professional judgment, the corporation is attempting, in good faith, to comply with the standards for approval of the American Bar Association and is making reasonable progress toward meeting them` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the corporation filed a copy of the report with the Secretary of Education and with the Attorney General` IS A BOOLEAN

-- "Notwithstanding the foregoing provisions, any corporation conducting a law school, which has its principal place of operation in Delaware,
-- and which intends to meet the standards of approval of the American Bar Association, may, after it has been in actual operation for not less
-- than 1 year, retain at its own expense a dean or dean emeritus of a law school fully approved by the American Bar Association to make an
-- on-site inspection and report ... Such dean or dean emeritus shall be chosen by the Attorney General from a panel of 3 deans whose names
-- are presented to the Attorney General as being willing to serve. One such dean on this panel shall be nominated by the trustees of said
-- law school corporation; another dean shall be nominated by a committee of the Student Bar Association of said law school; and the other
-- dean shall be nominated by a committee of lawyers who are parents of students attending such law school. If any of the above-named groups
-- cannot find a dean, it may substitute 2 full professors of accredited law schools for the dean it is entitled to nominate ... If the dean so
-- retained shall report in writing that, in such dean's professional judgment, the corporation is attempting, in good faith, to comply with
-- the standards for approval of the American Bar Association and is making reasonable progress toward meeting such standards, the corporation
-- may file a copy of the report with the Secretary of Education and with the Attorney General. Any corporation which complies with these
-- provisions by filing such report shall be deemed to have temporary approval from the State and shall be entitled to amend its certificate
-- of incorporation to authorize the granting of standard academic law degrees." The year in actual operation is counted from the date it began.
-- src:282 | Notwithstanding the foregoing provisions, any corporation conducting a law school, which has its principal place of operation in Delaware, and which intends to meet the standards of approval of the American Bar Association, may, after it has been in actual operation for not less than 1 year, retain at its own expense a dean or dean emeritus of a law school fully approved by the American Bar Association to make an on-site inspection and report concerning the progress of the corporation toward meeting the standards for approval by the American Bar Association. Such dean or dean emeritus shall be chosen by the Attorney General from a panel of 3 deans whose names are presented to the Attorney General as being willing to serve. One such dean on this panel shall be nominated by the trustees of said law school corporation; another dean shall be nominated by a committee of the Student Bar Association of said law school; and the other dean shall be nominated by a committee of lawyers who are parents of students attending such law school. If any of the above-named groups cannot find a dean, it may substitute 2 full professors of accredited law schools for the dean it is entitled to nominate, and in such a case if the Attorney General chooses 1 of such professors, such professor shall serve the function of a dean as herein prescribed. If the dean so retained shall report in writing that, in such dean’s professional judgment, the corporation is attempting, in good faith, to comply with the standards for approval of the American Bar Association and is making reasonable progress toward meeting such standards, the corporation may file a copy of the report with the Secretary of Education and with the Attorney General. Any corporation which complies with these provisions by filing such report shall be deemed to have temporary approval from the State and shall be entitled to amend its certificate of incorporation to authorize the granting of standard academic law degrees. Thereafter, until the law school operated by the corporation is approved by the American Bar Association, the corporation shall file once during each academic year a new report, in the same manner as the first report. If, at any time, the corporation fails to file such a report, or if the dean retained to render such report states that, in such dean’s opinion, the corporation is not continuing to make reasonable progress toward accreditation, the Attorney General, at the request of the Secretary of Education, may file a complaint in the Court of Chancery to suspend said temporary approval and degree-granting power until a further report is filed by a dean or dean emeritus of an accredited law school that the school has resumed its progress towards meeting the standards for approval. Upon approval of the law school by the American Bar Association, temporary approval shall become final, and shall no longer be subject to suspension or vacation under this section.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 125 (src:282)
GIVEN f IS A `s 125 Facts about a law school corporation`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 125 the law school corporation has temporary approval from the State` f MEANS
        f's `the corporation is conducting a law school which has its principal place of operation in Delaware`
    AND f's `the corporation intends to meet the standards of approval of the American Bar Association`
    AND (f's `the date the corporation retained the dean` AT LEAST (`the date` (`period in years` 1) `after` (f's `the date the corporation began actual operation`)))
    AND f's `the corporation retained the dean at its own expense to make an on-site inspection and report`
    AND f's `the dean or dean emeritus is of a law school fully approved by the American Bar Association`
    AND f's `the dean was chosen by the Attorney General from a panel of 3 deans nominated one each by the trustees of the corporation, a committee of the Student Bar Association and a committee of lawyers who are parents of students, with 2 full professors of accredited law schools substituted for any dean a group could not find`
    AND f's `the dean reported in writing that, in the dean's professional judgment, the corporation is attempting, in good faith, to comply with the standards for approval of the American Bar Association and is making reasonable progress toward meeting them`
    AND f's `the corporation filed a copy of the report with the Secretary of Education and with the Attorney General`

-- "Thereafter, until the law school operated by the corporation is approved by the American Bar Association, the corporation shall file once
-- during each academic year a new report, in the same manner as the first report."
-- src:282 | Thereafter, until the law school operated by the corporation is approved by the American Bar Association, the corporation shall file once during each academic year a new report, in the same manner as the first report. …
@ref 8 Del. C. § 125 (src:282)
GIVEN `the corporation has temporary approval from the State` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the law school has been approved by the American Bar Association` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 125 the corporation must file a new report once during the academic year` `the corporation has temporary approval from the State` `the law school has been approved by the American Bar Association` MEANS
        `the corporation has temporary approval from the State`
    AND (NOT `the law school has been approved by the American Bar Association`)

-- "If, at any time, the corporation fails to file such a report, or if the dean retained to render such report states that, in such dean's
-- opinion, the corporation is not continuing to make reasonable progress toward accreditation, the Attorney General, at the request of the
-- Secretary of Education, may file a complaint in the Court of Chancery to suspend said temporary approval and degree-granting power until a
-- further report is filed by a dean or dean emeritus of an accredited law school that the school has resumed its progress towards meeting the
-- standards for approval." The Attorney General's power; the corporation's liability to the complaint. Whether the Court suspends is the Court's.
-- src:282 | If, at any time, the corporation fails to file such a report, or if the dean retained to render such report states that, in such dean’s opinion, the corporation is not continuing to make reasonable progress toward accreditation, the Attorney General, at the request of the Secretary of Education, may file a complaint in the Court of Chancery to suspend said temporary approval and degree-granting power until a further report is filed by a dean or dean emeritus of an accredited law school that the school has resumed its progress towards meeting the standards for approval. …
@ref 8 Del. C. § 125 (src:282)
GIVEN `the corporation has temporary approval from the State` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the law school has been approved by the American Bar Association` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the corporation fails to file such a report` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the dean retained to render the report states that, in the dean's opinion, the corporation is not continuing to make reasonable progress toward accreditation` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Secretary of Education has requested the Attorney General to file a complaint` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 125 the Attorney General may file a complaint in the Court of Chancery to suspend the temporary approval and degree-granting power` `the corporation has temporary approval from the State` `the law school has been approved by the American Bar Association` `the corporation fails to file such a report` `the dean retained to render the report states that, in the dean's opinion, the corporation is not continuing to make reasonable progress toward accreditation` `the Secretary of Education has requested the Attorney General to file a complaint` MEANS
        `the corporation has temporary approval from the State`
    AND (NOT `the law school has been approved by the American Bar Association`)
    AND (   `the corporation fails to file such a report`
         OR `the dean retained to render the report states that, in the dean's opinion, the corporation is not continuing to make reasonable progress toward accreditation`)
    AND `the Secretary of Education has requested the Attorney General to file a complaint`

-- "Upon approval of the law school by the American Bar Association, temporary approval shall become final, and shall no longer be subject
-- to suspension or vacation under this section."
-- src:282 | Upon approval of the law school by the American Bar Association, temporary approval shall become final, and shall no longer be subject to suspension or vacation under this section.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 125 (src:282)
GIVEN `the law school has been approved by the American Bar Association` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 125 the temporary approval has become final and is no longer subject to suspension or vacation` `the law school has been approved by the American Bar Association` MEANS
    `the law school has been approved by the American Bar Association`

§ `Section 126: banking power denied`

DECLARE `s 126(a) Kind of activity` IS ONE OF
    `issuing bills, notes, or other evidences of debt for circulation as money`
    `carrying on the business of receiving deposits of money`
    `any other activity`

-- "No corporation organized under this chapter shall possess the power of issuing bills, notes, or other evidences of debt for circulation as
-- money, or the power of carrying on the business of receiving deposits of money." For any other activity the subsection does not speak.
-- src:286 | (a) No corporation organized under this chapter shall possess the power of issuing bills, notes, or other evidences of debt for circulation as money, or the power of carrying on the business of receiving deposits of money.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 126(a) (src:286)
GIVEN `the corporation is organized under this chapter` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the activity` IS A `s 126(a) Kind of activity`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 126(a) the corporation possesses the power` `the corporation is organized under this chapter` `the activity` MEANS
    IF   NOT `the corporation is organized under this chapter`
    THEN NOTHING
    ELSE CONSIDER `the activity`
         WHEN `issuing bills, notes, or other evidences of debt for circulation as money` THEN JUST FALSE
         WHEN `carrying on the business of receiving deposits of money` THEN JUST FALSE
         WHEN `any other activity` THEN NOTHING

-- "Corporations organized under this chapter to buy, sell and otherwise deal in notes, open accounts and other similar evidences of debt, or to
-- loan money and to take notes, open accounts and other similar evidences of debt as collateral security therefor, shall not be deemed to be
-- engaging in the business of banking."
-- src:287 | (b) Corporations organized under this chapter to buy, sell and otherwise deal in notes, open accounts and other similar evidences of debt, or to loan money and to take notes, open accounts and other similar evidences of debt as collateral security therefor, shall not be deemed to be engaging in the business of banking.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 126(b) (src:287)
GIVEN `the corporation is organized to buy, sell and otherwise deal in notes, open accounts and other similar evidences of debt` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the corporation is organized to loan money and to take notes, open accounts and other similar evidences of debt as collateral security for the loan` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 126(b) the corporation is deemed to be engaging in the business of banking` `the corporation is organized to buy, sell and otherwise deal in notes, open accounts and other similar evidences of debt` `the corporation is organized to loan money and to take notes, open accounts and other similar evidences of debt as collateral security for the loan` MEANS
    IF   `the corporation is organized to buy, sell and otherwise deal in notes, open accounts and other similar evidences of debt`
         OR `the corporation is organized to loan money and to take notes, open accounts and other similar evidences of debt as collateral security for the loan`
    THEN JUST FALSE
    ELSE NOTHING

§ `Section 127: private foundation`

DECLARE `s 127 Tax` IS ONE OF
    `the tax imposed by 26 U.S.C. section 4941 (taxes on self-dealing)`
    `the tax imposed by 26 U.S.C. section 4942 (taxes on failure to distribute income)`
    `the tax imposed by 26 U.S.C. section 4943 (taxes on excess business holdings)`
    `the tax imposed by 26 U.S.C. section 4944 (taxes on investments which jeopardize charitable purpose)`
    `the tax imposed by 26 U.S.C. section 4945 (taxable expenditures)`
    `the tax imposed by a corresponding provision of a subsequent United States internal revenue law`
    `a tax of any other kind`

-- "A corporation of this State which is a private foundation under the United States internal revenue laws and whose certificate of
-- incorporation does not expressly provide that this section shall not apply to it is required to act or to refrain from acting so as not to
-- subject itself to the taxes imposed by 26 U.S.C. § 4941 (relating to taxes on self-dealing), § 4942 (relating to taxes on failure to
-- distribute income), § 4943 (relating to taxes on excess business holdings), § 4944 (relating to taxes on investments which jeopardize
-- charitable purpose), or § 4945 (relating to taxable expenditures), or corresponding provisions of any subsequent United States internal
-- revenue law." Whether the corporation is a private foundation is federal law (not among the inputs): a fact. A tax of another kind: not covered.
-- out of range: 26 U.S.C. sections 4941 to 4945 and the private foundation status (federal law, not among the inputs): a plain fact.
-- src:291 | A corporation of this State which is a private foundation under the United States internal revenue laws and whose certificate of incorporation does not expressly provide that this section shall not apply to it is required to act or to refrain from acting so as not to subject itself to the taxes imposed by 26 U.S.C. § 4941 (relating to taxes on self-dealing), § 4942 (relating to taxes on failure to distribute income), § 4943 (relating to taxes on excess business holdings), § 4944 (relating to taxes on investments which jeopardize charitable purpose), or § 4945 (relating to taxable expenditures), or corresponding provisions of any subsequent United States internal revenue law.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 127 (src:291)
GIVEN `the corporation is a corporation of this State` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the corporation is a private foundation under the United States internal revenue laws` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the certificate of incorporation expressly provides that this section shall not apply to it` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the tax` IS A `s 127 Tax`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 127 the corporation is required to act or to refrain from acting so as not to subject itself to the tax` `the corporation is a corporation of this State` `the corporation is a private foundation under the United States internal revenue laws` `the certificate of incorporation expressly provides that this section shall not apply to it` `the tax` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the tax`
    WHEN `a tax of any other kind` THEN NOTHING
    OTHERWISE JUST (   `the corporation is a corporation of this State`
                    AND `the corporation is a private foundation under the United States internal revenue laws`
                    AND (NOT `the certificate of incorporation expressly provides that this section shall not apply to it`))
